00:35:44.530 --> 00:35:45.874
- Yes.

00:35:45.874 --> 00:35:48.766
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:35:53.586 --> 00:35:55.040
[END PLAYBACK]

00:35:55.040 --> 00:35:57.132
JOEL HEGG: OK, so
just to summarize,

00:35:57.132 --> 00:35:58.590
what you saw there
was a few things

00:35:58.590 --> 00:36:00.810
that I talked about in action.

00:36:00.810 --> 00:36:02.370
We showed our AI.

00:36:02.370 --> 00:36:05.550
So when the user says, ask
eBay for a Kate Spade bag,

00:36:05.550 --> 00:36:09.120
our NLU will try and
parse that input.

00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:10.830
It will go to our
Knowledge Graph

00:36:10.830 --> 00:36:13.380
and try and find additional
attributes about Kate Spade

00:36:13.380 --> 00:36:17.120
bags, so including
color and style.

00:36:17.120 --> 00:36:19.450
It uses our Dialogue
Manager to process

00:36:19.450 --> 00:36:21.530
the output of the NLU
and the Knowledge Graph

00:36:21.530 --> 00:36:24.770
and then takes the content that
it has internally and formats

00:36:24.770 --> 00:36:26.420
responses.

00:36:26.420 --> 00:36:28.220
It uses the AI memory
so that it remembers,

00:36:28.220 --> 00:36:31.720
across these three turns,
what the user inputted.

00:36:31.720 --> 00:36:36.120
And then, finally,
it returns results.

00:36:36.120 --> 00:36:38.930
We use the Fabric API
so that we can translate

00:36:38.930 --> 00:36:42.440
from the conversational
platform, Google Assistant's

00:36:42.440 --> 00:36:45.010
request response
format, into the format

00:36:45.010 --> 00:36:48.380
that our AI
understands internally.

00:36:48.380 --> 00:36:50.700
Then, we factor in channel
and device capabilities.

00:36:50.700 --> 00:36:55.070
So the initial interaction
was through Google Home,

00:36:55.070 --> 00:36:57.560
and it's a completely
voice-based interface.

00:36:57.560 --> 00:37:00.940
And we had to tailor the
response with the expectation

00:37:00.940 --> 00:37:03.260
that the user didn't
have a screen to look at.

00:37:03.260 --> 00:37:06.317
So at the very end, when we
had results to present them,

00:37:06.317 --> 00:37:08.900
we asked them, do they want to
transfer this conversation over

00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:10.820
to their phone on
Google Assistant?

00:37:10.820 --> 00:37:12.270
And that's what happened there.

00:37:12.270 --> 00:37:16.460
We loaded the final
results of our AI memory.

00:37:16.460 --> 00:37:19.182
And when the user came
in from their phone,

00:37:19.182 --> 00:37:21.640
we presented them with an ID
card showing them the results.

00:37:25.140 --> 00:37:29.009
So, in summary, eBay ShopBot
is an intelligent and trusted

00:37:29.009 --> 00:37:30.800
personal shopping
assistant available today

00:37:30.800 --> 00:37:33.970
for Google Assistant
and Facebook Messenger.

00:37:33.970 --> 00:37:39.310
We ran into issues that caused
us to not use Dialogflow

00:37:39.310 --> 00:37:40.900
or the traditional
way you'd integrate

00:37:40.900 --> 00:37:42.700
with a conversational platform.

00:37:42.700 --> 00:37:45.470
We built our own AI stack.

00:37:45.470 --> 00:37:47.560
And we have a request
response format

00:37:47.560 --> 00:37:51.100
that we translate external
formats into so we can handle

00:37:51.100 --> 00:37:54.220
them in a platform-neutral way.

00:37:54.220 --> 00:37:57.875
We built this on
Google Cloud to help

00:37:57.875 --> 00:37:59.500
made this entire
architecture possible.

00:38:02.780 --> 00:38:04.420
All right, thank you.

00:38:04.420 --> 00:38:07.470
